From: frapercan <frapercan1@alum.us.es>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:47:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Fail the pipeline when tasks were discarded

A task that failed in a worker was logged and dropped (nack without
requeue), and start() still returned normally. Callers could not tell that
results were missing: FANTASIA lost a whole lookup batch to an alignment
error and still exited with 0.

Count discarded tasks in a multiprocessing.Value shared with the worker
processes: inserting-queue failures, and computing-queue failures that
failed again after the retry. After post-processing, start() raises
TaskFailuresError if any task was discarded, so partial results are still
written. ValueError in process() remains an intentional skip.

Add fail_on_task_errors (default True) to only log a warning instead.
---
 protein_information_system/config/config.yaml |  5 ++
 protein_information_system/tasks/queue.py     | 32 ++++++++
 tests/tasks/test_queue_task_initializer.py    | 73 ++++++++++++++++++-
